    "summary": "The NAND Flash market is expected to enter a downward pricing cycle as supply continues to expand, prompting TrendForce to lower its 2027 NAND Flash revenue forecast to approximately US$419.3 billion. Brands are expected to reduce NAND Flash capacity specifications across their product portfolios to keep bill-of-materials (BOM) costs under control. On the supply side, however, some manufacturers will continue expanding production capacity, while process technology migrations at other suppliers will further increase bit output. DRAM bit supply is expected to continue growing year-over-year as major manufacturers expand wafer capacity and migrate to more advanced process technologies.",
