    "summary": "TrendForce’s latest quarterly report, “LED Display Module Quarterly Cost and Market Analysis,” reveals that PCB cost increases in the fourth quarter of 2026 have driven up manufacturing costs for COB and SMD LED displays. This increase was primarily driven by high-value-added applications such as AI computing and high-speed substrates absorbing much of the upstream electronic-grade glass fiber cloth production capacity. Furthermore, lengthy capacity expansion cycles for glass fiber cloth have limited additional supply in the near term, keeping inventory levels low. Based on current supply-demand conditions for upstream PCB materials, high-end PCB prices are expected to continue rising, albeit at a slower pace.",
