      "engineeringConclusion": "The PQ2 uses KIOXIA’s 4-bit-per-cell QLC NAND with CMOS directly Bonded to Array (CBA) technology, which SSSTC says improves memory density, performance, and power efficiency. The drives are DRAM-less and use Host Memory Buffer (HMB) technology, which borrows a portion of system memory for work an onboard DRAM chip would typically handle. The 2280 card measures 80mm by 22mm and weighs up to 6g, and the 2230 card is 30mm long at up to 3g, sized for compact devices and embedded boards. Both lengths come in 512GB, 1TB, and 2TB capacities."
