    "publishedAt": "2026-11-25",
    "summary": "NRW, a €35 million ($38.4 million) initiative to develop and integrate a semiconductor-based quantum computer with up to 200 qubits. The initiative will run until the end of 2029 and receive 90 percent of its funding from German federal funds under the Coal Regions Investment Act, with the final ten percent coming from the State of North Rhine-Westphalia via Forschungszentrum Jülich Supercomputing Center (FZJ). Alongside the hardware, the project partners are also developing the software, hybrid quantum algorithms, and services for user support and training. Integrating the new semiconductor-based system into JUNIQ allows us to develop hybrid quantum-HPC workflows on a powerful and scalable platform and make them accessible to a broad user community.",
