    "publishedAt": "2026-11-25",
    "summary": "Scalable, resilient AI-ready infrastructure requires data center designers and operators to adopt an integrated strategy by engineering electrical distribution and liquid cooling as a unified system architecture from day one. While conventional enterprise data center racks historically drew under 10kW, next-generation clusters now routinely demand 40kW to over 140kW per rack . Once rack densities cross about 30kW to 40kW, traditional air cooling reaches a physical limit . Rather than attempting to reconcile mismatched electrical equipment and liquid cooling hardware in the field, operators can deploy standardized architectures tailored to specific facility parameters, whether retrofitting legacy space for liquid-assisted cooling at 40kW to 70kW per rack or constructing purpose-built facilities designed for 140+ kW per rack.",
    "whyItMatters": "立讯需要把重点放在整机柜、供电、散热、高速线缆和连接器，而不是只看 GPU 或服务器品牌。",
