    "summary": "While QumulusAI secures 2MW of colocation capacity French AI cloud provider Exaion has secured a US customer under a four-year contract, while US-based AI cloud company QumulusAI has secured 2MW of colocation capacity. Under Exaion's agreement, it will provide GPU-as-a-Service in a 100 percent take-or-pay contract valued at $79 million. Spanning 4,000 sq ft (372 sqm), the Tier II quality facility offers 780kW of capacity. QumulusAI said the capacity is expected to be ready for service by the end of 2026, and the company has a right of first offer on a further 9.6MW at the site.",
