    "summary": "Base-build commissioning for first 75MW completed Applied Digital has made its first 25MW data hall ready for service at the company's Polaris Forge 2 data center campus in Harwood, North Dakota. CEO says firms must earn the right to launch new projects as it plots expansion into Europe The remaining 50MW will now go through fit-out and customer delivery. The Polaris Forge 2 data center campus is largely leased by an unnamed investment-grade hyperscaler, which signed a 15-year 200MW lease in October 2025 , and has right of first refusal on up to 800MW more capacity at the site. Earlier this week, Applied Digital revealed it had secured another customer, signing an 18-year capacity agreement with another investment-grade hyperscaler with a base-term revenue of $5.4bn , increasing to $12.7bn if all renewal options are exercised over the potential 33 years.",
